<InfoLayout title="Bang My Twister — archive record" description="A rights-aware record of a former Max for Live and controller project associated with this domain." canonicalPath="/legacy/bang-my-twister/" kicker="Historical resource" lede="An old controller-project reference, documented without presenting the current publisher as its creator." noindex={true}>
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">What can be checked</h2>
  <p>A DJ TechTools mapping record remains available for mapping ID 2929 and links the historic controller context to this domain. That external record is the appropriate place to inspect its current availability. Auspicious Music does not mirror the mapping or former Max for Live files.</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn--quiet" href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">Open the DJ TechTools record</a></p>
  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>External record</dt><dd>DJ TechTools mapping 2929</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Former authorship</dt><dd>Not claimed by the current publisher</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Local download</dt><dd>Not offered</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Compatibility</dt><dd>Not tested by the current publisher</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Why the old URL remains useful</h2>
  <p>A person following an old music-technology reference receives an explanation and the strongest surviving external source. They are not redirected to a generic homepage and are not told that an untested device is current.</p>

  <h2>A current, original guide</h2>
  <p>The article <a href="/ableton/midi-fighter-twister-review/">Design the mapping before the knobs</a> offers a controller-agnostic method for building and documenting an Ableton mapping. It explicitly does not claim to be a completed Twister hardware review.</p>

  <h2>Sources used for this record</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">DJ TechTools mapping archive</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://auspiciousmusic.com/" rel="noopener">Internet Archive capture index for the former domain</a></li>
  </ul>
</InfoLayout>
